      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] `common/system.c` is shared across all `CONFIG_MPU` targets (including STM32, MCHP, and RISC-V), whereas RAM lock (`CONFIG_NPCX_RAM_LOCK`) is specific to NPCX and gated on `system_is_locked()` inside `mpu_enable()` in `zephyr/shim/core/cortex-m/mpu.c`.\n\nLogging `\"Skip RAM lock configuration\"` unconditionally here will print a misleading message on non-NPCX targets where RAM lock does not exist, and duplicates the `system_is_locked()` check. Consider gating this log on `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NPCX_RAM_LOCK)` or moving it into the `#if defined(CONFIG_NPCX_RAM_LOCK)` block in `mpu_enable()`.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/1be31127-4393-412c-81c7-4698832019a0)",
